{
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "lib": ["ES2022", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    /*
     * Deliberately empty. `types` used to be `["vite/client"]`, which is a hard
     * entry-point type library: when `vite` was not resolvable from this package
     * TypeScript raised a fatal `TS2688: Cannot find type definition file for
     * 'vite/client'` and no source file could be checked at all. An empty array
     * also stops TypeScript auto-including every `@types/*` package it happens
     * to find, so what this program sees is only what it explicitly imports plus
     * the ambient declarations in `src/env.d.ts`.
     *
     * See src/env.d.ts and specs/003-rota-custos-web/spec.md § Defect.
     */
    "types": [],
    "noEmit": true,
    "baseUrl": ".",
    "paths": {
      "@/*": ["./src/*"]
    }
  },
  "include": ["src"]
}
